If this is a @decimal, the exponent can only be an @int[integer].¨calc.quo½The dividend of the quotient.¼The divisor of the quotient.¨calc.rem¾The dividend of the remainder.½The divisor of the remainder.¯calc.rem-euclid©calc.root¨radicandÙ#The expression to take the root of.±The value of $n$.ªcalc.round´The number to round.¦digitsÙ’If positive, the number of decimal places.

If negative, the number of significant integer digits that should be
removed before the decimal point.¨calc.sinÙ"The angle whose sine to calculate.©calc.sinhÙ8The hyperbolic angle whose hyperbolic sine to calculate.©calc.sqrtÙ@The number whose square root to calculate. Must be non-negative.¨calc.tanÙ%The angle whose tangent to calculate.©calc.tanhÙ;The hyperbolic angle whose hyperbolic tangent to calculate.ªcalc.trunc¦cancelÙ1The content over which the line should be placed.¦lengthÚ,The length of the line, relative to the length of the diagonal spanning
the whole element being "cancelled". A value of `{100%}` would then have
